From 2e8e84a537c1b7321879deab660978d765559028 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:06:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dwc2d: gamepad sticks count only once near the middle;
 DragonRise button order

A DragonRise pad (0079:0011) lists X four times. If an unused one rests
at one end, it held D-pad LEFT from the first report on (redox-rpi Pi
test row 416). A stick value now counts, as an axis and for the D-pad,
only after it has once been within 25 % of the middle, and values near
the middle are sent as 0 (the pad rested at -129).

The pad's buttons are in SNES order: a table by USB id maps them by
position as SDL does, so Select and Start are BACK and START instead of
LS and RS. With the input log on, dwc2d logs each new raw report.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
